problem:
The 83 interns from the Animath internship each choose an activity for the free afternoon from 5 proposed activities. We know that:

$\triangleright$ Shopping has been at least as popular as Laser Game;

$\Delta$ Movie tickets are sold in lots of 6;

$\Delta$ At most 5 students go to the beach;

$\triangleright$ At most one student has visited a Romanesque church.

When writing the list of activities in alphabetical order, one writes the number of students corresponding to each activity. How many different lists of numbers could have been written?

